  <Row><Cell>merc_provider_capon</Cell><Cell>His Lordship is at your service.</Cell><Cell>大人願為你效力。</Cell></Row>


  <Row><Cell>merc_info_returning</Cell><Cell>Your mercenaries are on their way.</Cell><Cell>你的傭兵正在趕來的路上。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>ui_mercenary_type_return</Cell><Cell>Recall my men.</Cell><Cell>召回我的人。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>merc_henry_type_return</Cell><Cell>Send word to my men. I need them back.</Cell><Cell>給我的人捎個信,我需要他們回來。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>merc_provider_type_return</Cell><Cell>Consider it done. I'll send a runner right away.</Cell><Cell>就當辦妥了,我馬上派人送信去。</Cell></Row>

  <Row><Cell>ui_mercenary_heal_yourselves</Cell><Cell>Patch yourselves up (20 groschen).</Cell><Cell>把自己包紮一下。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>merc_heal_henry_1</Cell><Cell>Here's 20 groschen, patch yourselves up. You look terrible.</Cell><Cell>拿著這些用品,把自己包紮一下。你們這模樣真是慘不忍睹。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>merc_heal_merc</Cell><Cell>That'll cover bandages and drink. We'll be right as rain.</Cell><Cell>我們盡力而為,老大,不過有個正經郎中在就更好了。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>merc_info_merc_healed</Cell><Cell>Your mercenaries have been healed.</Cell><Cell>你的傭兵已經治療完畢。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>merc_info_nobody_injured</Cell><Cell>Nobody needs healing right now.</Cell><Cell>Nobody needs healing right now.</Cell></Row>


  <Row><Cell>merc_test_bark_string</Cell><Cell>This is a test. I like cheese.</Cell><Cell>這是個測試。我喜歡起司。</Cell></Row>

  <Row><Cell>a614a_story1</Cell><Cell>I don't fear death, I fear soup made by someone confident.</Cell><Cell>我不怕死,我怕的是一個自信滿滿的人煮的湯。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story2</Cell><Cell>I once trusted a man who said shortcut, we arrived older.</Cell><Cell>我曾經信了一個說「抄近路」的人,結果我們到的時候都老了幾歲。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story3</Cell><Cell>A priest, a butcher and a taxman walk into a tavern - everyone hides their groschen.</Cell><Cell>一個神父、一個屠夫和一個收稅官走進酒館——所有人都把格羅申藏了起來。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story4</Cell><Cell>He said he knew the road, the road is agreed.</Cell><Cell>他說他認得路,那條路現在也同意了。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story5</Cell><Cell>My uncle survived three wars and died arguing with a goose.</Cell><Cell>我叔叔挺過了三場戰爭,最後卻死於跟一隻鵝吵架。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story6</Cell><Cell>A rich man calls it patience, a poor man calls it waiting.</Cell><Cell>有錢人管這叫耐心,窮人管這叫苦等。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story7</Cell><Cell>Nothing humbles a man faster, than trying to look brave while slipping in mud.</Cell><Cell>沒有什麼比在泥地裡滑倒還想裝勇敢更能讓人謙卑的了。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story8</Cell><Cell>I don't drink to forget, I drink because the water ... looks ambitious.</Cell><Cell>我喝酒不是為了忘記,而是因為那水……看起來太有野心了。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story9</Cell><Cell>I prayed for guidance and got rain. Well, close enough.</Cell><Cell>我祈求指引,結果下了雨。好吧,也算差不多了。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story10</Cell><Cell>A man who says trust me, has already stolen something.</Cell><Cell>一個說「相信我」的人,通常已經偷了點什麼。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story11</Cell><Cell>The woods are peaceful, until you remember, everything in them eats without a spoon.</Cell><Cell>森林很寧靜,直到你想起,裡頭的一切都不用湯匙進食。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story12</Cell><Cell>I would rather sleep in a ditch, than in a castle with politics.</Cell><Cell>我寧可睡在溝渠裡,也不願睡在充滿權謀的城堡中。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story13</Cell><Cell>Never insult a cook before breakfast, that's how legends become warnings.</Cell><Cell>早飯前千萬別羞辱廚子,傳奇就是這樣變成警世故事的。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story14</Cell><Cell>Henry went to deliver a message and invented six unrelated crimes on the way.</Cell><Cell>亨利本來只是去送個信,結果一路上莫名其妙惹出六樁無關的案子。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story15</Cell><Cell>I saw a man walk into the Kuttenberg mines sober, that was his first mistake.</Cell><Cell>我看見一個人清醒著走進庫特納霍拉的礦坑,那就是他犯的第一個錯。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story16</Cell><Cell>Kuttenberg has fine walls, shame about the people inside them.</Cell><Cell>庫特納霍拉的城牆很堅固,可惜牆裡的人不怎麼樣。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story17</Cell><Cell>Henry of Skalitz, blacksmith, messenger, detective, idiot magnet.</Cell><Cell>斯卡利采的亨利,鐵匠、信使、偵探,還有招惹傻瓜的磁鐵。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story18</Cell><Cell>I met a peaceful monk once, he was sharpening something.</Cell><Cell>我曾遇過一個「安詳」的僧侶,他當時正在磨什麼東西。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story19</Cell><Cell>A man with clean armor near Kuttenberg is either rich or recently replaced.</Cell><Cell>在庫特納霍拉附近穿著乾淨盔甲的人,不是有錢就是剛換了條命。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story20</Cell><Cell>He said it was a simple job, was henry's speech for bring armor and a priest.</Cell><Cell>他說這是件簡單差事,亨利這麼說就代表得帶上盔甲和神父了。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story21</Cell><Cell>I have guarded caravans safer, than one of henry's polite conversations.</Cell><Cell>我護送過的商隊都比亨利一場「客氣的談話」還安全。</Cell></Row>
  <Row><Cell>a614a_story22</Cell><Cell>Henry, you have the rare gift of making armed men look like paperwork.</Cell><Cell>亨利,你有種罕見的本事,能把全副武裝的人搞得跟文書作業一樣麻煩。</Cell></Row>





